This product is a Rust port of, and redistributes material from, two
MIT-licensed JavaScript libraries by Guillaume Plique (Yomguithereal).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. mnemonist — https://github.com/Yomguithereal/mnemonist
   Copyright (c) 2016 Guillaume Plique (Yomguithereal)
   Licence: MIT, reproduced verbatim in LICENSE-MNEMONIST

   The data structures in `crates/mnemonist-core` are ports of this
   library's implementations. Its published test suite is redistributed
   **unmodified** under `tests/original/`, byte-for-byte identical to the
   upstream release and verified by `sha256sum -c tests/SHA256SUMS`; it is
   the equivalence evidence this port rests on, and is not the work of this
   project. A vendored copy of the library itself is kept under
   `bench/upstream/` so both sides of a benchmark or a differential fuzz run
   execute the real upstream code rather than a description of it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. obliterator — https://github.com/Yomguithereal/obliterator
   Copyright (c) 2017-2021 Guillaume Plique (Yomguithereal)
   Licence: MIT, reproduced verbatim in LICENSE-OBLITERATOR

   `mnemonist` depends on this library for its iteration primitives, so
   porting `mnemonist` required porting them too. Two are reimplemented
   here, both against version 2.0.5:

     obliterator/iterator  ->  crates/mnemonist-core/src/cursor/
     obliterator/foreach   ->  crates/mnemonist-napi/src/foreach.rs

   Its error strings are reproduced exactly, because upstream's own tests
   assert on them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream carries no per-file copyright or SPDX headers. Each ported module
in this repository names the upstream file it derives from in its own
documentation, which exceeds that obligation and costs nothing.
